@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api
@token = PEGAR_EL_TOKEN_DEL_LOGIN

### Registro publico -> 201, siempre ASSISTANT
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "doc_type": "DNI", "doc_number": "40111222",
  "name": "Ana", "surname": "Perez",
  "email": "ana@test.com", "password": "12345678",
  "telephone": "3411112222"
}

### B1 - Intento de escalada de privilegios
# Se manda role: ADMIN. Tiene que volver "role": "ASSISTANT".
# El campo ni existe en el DTO de entrada: Zod lo descarta.
POST {{baseUrl}}/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "role": "ADMIN",
  "doc_type": "DNI", "doc_number": "40999888",
  "name": "Escalada", "surname": "Test",
  "email": "escalada2@test.com", "password": "12345678",
  "telephone": "3419998888"
}

### Listado completo -> solo ADMIN (401 sin token, 403 con token comun)
GET {{baseUrl}}/users
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Perfil propio -> propio o ADMIN
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### Cargar CUIT (requisito para ser organizador)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/users/1
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "cuit": "20401112223" }

### Promover a ORGANISER -> solo ADMIN
# Sin CUIT cargado devuelve 400 con el motivo.
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/users/1/role
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "role": "ORGANISER" }
